    <div class="about__content animate-in">
      <p>
        I'm a software engineer with a deep interest in machine learning, quantitative research,
        and building things that matter. I graduated from the
        <a href="https://www.unc.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill</a>
        in December 2025 with dual degrees in Statistics &amp; Analytics and Applied Mathematics,
        plus a minor in Entrepreneurship.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work spans from deploying production ML pipelines at Fidelity Investments to developing
        computer vision models for neurobiology research at the NIH. I co-founded
        <a href="https://www.ai-unc.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AI@UNC</a>, Carolina's
        first faculty-mentored AI research organization (400+ members), where I led the development of
        NeuroSpark -- an AI-powered VR system for awake craniotomy procedures.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of engineering, I've led a student-run escape room company as CEO, competed in
        quantitative trading, and presented research internationally at Oxford University.
        I'm driven by curiosity and care about work that sits at the intersection of
        rigorous engineering and real-world impact.
      </p>
